    <string name="help_title">How to use</string>
    <string name="help_done">Done</string>
    <string name="help_find_title">Find text on Android</string>
    <string name="help_find_body">Enter a word or phrase, then point the camera at readable printed Latin text. Matching ignores case and finds substrings within each OCR line; phrases do not cross lines. %1$s No match means none was recognized, not proof of absence.</string>
    <string name="help_lists_title">Search lists</string>
    <string name="help_lists_body">Create one entry per line; all entries are searched at once, and spaces within an entry stay part of its phrase. Selecting a list replaces the manual search. Editing the manual query returns to manual search.</string>
    <string name="help_preview_title">Preview and images</string>
    <string name="help_preview_body">The keyboard or open Search lists hide the preview. Dismiss the keyboard or close lists to see it; compact windows may need more space. Freeze frame keeps one image until Resume live. Import one JPEG, PNG, or WebP image; Return to camera exits it. OCR runs with the bundled on-device model. When you import, the system photo picker supplies the image. Copied text goes to the system clipboard, and sharing opens the system share sheet. Android saves search settings; device backup settings may affect saved app data. Images and OCR results stay in memory and are discarded when the app is backgrounded or the screen is recreated. An open photo picker can still complete after you return.</string>
    <string name="help_preview_scan_area">The optional scan area restricts live matches to fully contained words and phrases; it does not crop capture. Frozen, imported, and shared images use the whole source. Freeze, Import, backgrounding, or recreation resets the area.</string>
    <string name="help_colour_title">Colour and sharing on Android</string>
    <string name="help_colour_body">%1$s The selected colour applies to manual search. Each list entry gets a stable labelled colour across previews and shared images; open Search results to see each entry and its current count. Android saves the query, lists, selection, and colour. Share image is available for frozen or imported images; it prepares a temporary highlighted PNG and opens the system share sheet. Opening it does not confirm delivery or save to your gallery; the chosen app controls what happens next.</string>
    <string name="help_ios_title">iOS</string>
    <string name="help_ios_body">Query, lists, and colour are kept in memory only. Camera OCR, image import, and image sharing are unavailable in this build.</string>
